Track the minimum, maximum and total in one pass, then subtract the minimum and maximum from the total and divide by `n - 2`. This works because the salaries are unique, so exactly one employee holds the minimum and one holds the maximum.

The starter is a plain function rather than a class, so I kept that exact signature.

```typescript
function average(salary: number[]): number {
    let mn = Infinity, mx = -Infinity, sum = 0;
    for (const s of salary) {
        if (s < mn) mn = s;
        if (s > mx) mx = s;
        sum += s;
    }
    return (sum - mn - mx) / (salary.length - 2);
};
```

