To test collinearity, I use the cross product against the first two points. For each point `i` from index 2 onward, I check that `(x1-x0)*(yi-y0) - (y1-y0)*(xi-x0) == 0`. If any point gives a nonzero value, the points are not on one line. Using the cross product avoids division, so vertical lines need no special case. The values stay within about 4·10^8, well inside safe integer range.

```typescript
function checkStraightLine(coordinates: number[][]): boolean {
    const [x0, y0] = coordinates[0];
    const dx = coordinates[1][0] - x0;
    const dy = coordinates[1][1] - y0;
    for (let i = 2; i < coordinates.length; i++) {
        const ex = coordinates[i][0] - x0;
        const ey = coordinates[i][1] - y0;
        if (dx * ey - dy * ex !== 0) return false;
    }
    return true;
};
```

