Since n is at most 250, brute force over all pairs works. For each pair (a, b) with 1 ≤ a, b ≤ n, compute a² + b² and check whether it is a perfect square c² with c ≤ n. Each ordered pair that passes is counted once, so (3,4,5) and (4,3,5) both count. That is about 62,500 iterations.

```typescript
function countTriples(n: number): number {
    let count = 0;
    for (let a = 1; a <= n; a++) {
        for (let b = 1; b <= n; b++) {
            const s = a * a + b * b;
            const c = Math.round(Math.sqrt(s));
            if (c <= n && c * c === s) count++;
        }
    }
    return count;
};
```

