I'll use a lazy increment array: `inc[i]` holds a pending increment for the element at index `i`, to be passed down to the element below it when `i` is popped.

- **push:** if the stack is not full, append `x` and set its pending increment to 0.
- **increment(k, val):** let `i = min(k, size) - 1`. If `i >= 0`, add `val` to `inc[i]`. This takes O(1).
- **pop:** if the stack is empty, return -1. Otherwise take the top index `i`, compute `res = stack[i] + inc[i]`, and add `inc[i]` to `inc[i-1]` when `i > 0`. Then remove the top and return `res`.

The class uses a plain array plus a size counter, with `inc` preallocated to `maxSize`.

```typescript
class CustomStack {
    private stack: number[];
    private inc: number[];
    private size: number;
    private maxSize: number;

    constructor(maxSize: number) {
        this.maxSize = maxSize;
        this.stack = new Array(maxSize).fill(0);
        this.inc = new Array(maxSize).fill(0);
        this.size = 0;
    }

    push(x: number): void {
        if (this.size < this.maxSize) {
            this.stack[this.size] = x;
            this.inc[this.size] = 0;
            this.size++;
        }
    }

    pop(): number {
        if (this.size === 0) return -1;
        const i = this.size - 1;
        const res = this.stack[i] + this.inc[i];
        if (i > 0) this.inc[i - 1] += this.inc[i];
        this.inc[i] = 0;
        this.size--;
        return res;
    }

    increment(k: number, val: number): void {
        const i = Math.min(k, this.size) - 1;
        if (i >= 0) this.inc[i] += val;
    }
}
```

