For each point i, count the other points j by the normalized direction (dx, dy) from i to j. The largest count for any direction, plus 1 for point i itself, is the best line through i.

To normalize, divide dx and dy by their gcd. Then fix the sign so that dx > 0, or dx == 0 and dy > 0. Use the string `dx/dy` as the map key.

Coordinates go up to 1e4, so differences go up to 2e4 and the gcd approach is exact. With n ≤ 300 this is O(n²), which is fast enough.

The signature must stay `function maxPoints(points: number[][]): number`. If n ≤ 2, return n.

```typescript
function maxPoints(points: number[][]): number {
    const n = points.length;
    if (n <= 2) return n;
    const gcd = (a: number, b: number): number => {
        while (b !== 0) {
            const t = a % b;
            a = b;
            b = t;
        }
        return a;
    };
    let best = 1;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        const map = new Map<string, number>();
        let local = 0;
        for (let j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
            let dx = points[j][0] - points[i][0];
            let dy = points[j][1] - points[i][1];
            const g = gcd(Math.abs(dx), Math.abs(dy));
            dx /= g;
            dy /= g;
            if (dx < 0 || (dx === 0 && dy < 0)) {
                dx = -dx;
                dy = -dy;
            }
            const key = dx + "/" + dy;
            const c = (map.get(key) || 0) + 1;
            map.set(key, c);
            if (c > local) local = c;
        }
        if (local + 1 > best) best = local + 1;
    }
    return best;
};
```

