Approach: put every point in a set, keyed as `x * 40001 + y`. For each pair of points (i, j) with different x and different y, treat them as opposite corners of a rectangle. If the other two corners (x1, y2) and (x2, y1) are also in the set, the rectangle's area is |x1 - x2| * |y1 - y2|. Keep the minimum over all such pairs. With n ≤ 500 this is about 125,000 pairs, which is fast.

The largest key is 40000 * 40001 + 40000, about 1.6e9, which a JS number represents exactly. If no rectangle is found, return 0.

```typescript
function minAreaRect(points: number[][]): number {
    const M = 40001;
    const set = new Set<number>();
    for (const [x, y] of points) set.add(x * M + y);
    let best = Infinity;
    const n = points.length;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        const [x1, y1] = points[i];
        for (let j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
            const [x2, y2] = points[j];
            if (x1 === x2 || y1 === y2) continue;
            const area = Math.abs(x1 - x2) * Math.abs(y1 - y2);
            if (area >= best) continue;
            if (set.has(x1 * M + y2) && set.has(x2 * M + y1)) {
                best = area;
            }
        }
    }
    return best === Infinity ? 0 : best;
};
```

