2. Try removing each land cell in turn and recount islands. If any removal leaves a count other than 1, return 1. Removing the only land cell gives 0 islands, which is also disconnected, so a single-cell grid returns 1.
3. Otherwise return 2.

Removing any one cell can disconnect a grid only if that cell is an articulation point, and the brute-force recount covers this. The cost is 900 cells times a 900-cell flood fill, about 810k operations, which is fine.

