The approach is to give each letter a coefficient equal to the sum of its place values on the left side minus its place values in the result. The equation holds when the coefficient-weighted sum of the assigned digits is 0. Then backtrack over digit assignments.

Details:
- The example strings contain trailing spaces (e.g. "SEND "). The real tests probably don't, but I'll trim each word to be safe.
- A letter that is the first character of a word or of the result and belongs to a word longer than 1 character cannot be 0. A single-letter word may be 0, since "0" has no leading zero.
- Collect the distinct letters, with at most 10 of them. Backtrack by letter index with a used-digit mask and a running sum. At the end, check that the sum is 0.
- At most 10! = 3.6M leaves, which is fine.

Implementation:
- Compute `coef[c]` by iterating each word from its end with a multiplier of 10^i, adding for words and subtracting for the result.
- Mark `nonzero[c]` when the letter is at index 0 of a string with length > 1.
- `dfs(i, sum)` tries digits d from 0 to 9 that are unused and, if `nonzero`, d > 0, and returns true when `i == n` and `sum == 0`.

```typescript
function isSolvable(words: string[], result: string): boolean {
    const ws = words.map(w => w.trim());
    const res = result.trim();
    const coef: number[] = new Array(26).fill(0);
    const present: boolean[] = new Array(26).fill(false);
    const nonzero: boolean[] = new Array(26).fill(false);
    const process = (w: string, sign: number) => {
        let m = 1;
        for (let i = w.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            const c = w.charCodeAt(i) - 65;
            coef[c] += sign * m;
            present[c] = true;
            m *= 10;
        }
        if (w.length > 1) nonzero[w.charCodeAt(0) - 65] = true;
    };
    for (const w of ws) process(w, 1);
    process(res, -1);
    const letters: number[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < 26; i++) if (present[i]) letters.push(i);
    const n = letters.length;
    if (n > 10) return false;
    let used = 0;
    const dfs = (i: number, sum: number): boolean => {
        if (i === n) return sum === 0;
        const c = letters[i];
        for (let d = 0; d < 10; d++) {
            if (used & (1 << d)) continue;
            if (d === 0 && nonzero[c]) continue;
            used |= 1 << d;
            const ok = dfs(i + 1, sum + coef[c] * d);
            used &= ~(1 << d);
            if (ok) return true;
        }
        return false;
    };
    return dfs(0, 0);
};
```

